    "result_text": "The full suite is just the one acceptance test (only one test class exists), and it's green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `checkDigit` as the Luhn check digit computed over the digits of the owner's `customerCode`.\n\nChanges:\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `checkDigit` property (integer 0\u20139) to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains `getCheckDigit`/`setCheckDigit`.\n2. **`src/main/java/.../util/LuhnCheckDigit.java`** (new) \u2014 A small utility with `compute(String)` returning the Luhn check digit over the decimal digits in the string (ignoring non-digits like the `-` in `SMI-0007`), matching the algorithm the test replicates.\n3. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a MapStruct mapping that derives `checkDigit` from `owner.getCustomerCode()` (null-safe when the code is absent).\n\n`AcceptanceTest.coreCheckDigitIsLuhnOfCustomerCode` passes: **Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0 \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS**.",
